    "type": "question",
    "label": "",
    "prompt": "Use integration and the initial conditions to find the solution of $y''=\\sec^2 x$ with $y(0)=1$ and $y'(0)=1$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=1+x-\\ln(\\cos x)$",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}y''&=\\sec^2 x\\\\y'&=\\int\\sec^2 x\\,dx\\\\y'&=\\tan x+A\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $y'(0)=1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}1&=0+A\\\\A&=1\\\\y'&=\\tan x+1\\end{align*}$$\n$$\\begin{align*}y&=\\int(\\tan x+1)\\,dx\\\\y&=-\\ln|\\cos x|+x+B\\end{align*}$$\nUsing $y(0)=1$:\n$$\\begin{align*}1&=0+0+B\\\\B&=1\\\\y&=1+x-\\ln(\\cos x)\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
